# Crawl output is large binary screenshots plus multi-MB JSON, regenerable
# with `ux-crawl <url>`. The LENS (contrastive pairs and assertions) is the
# artifact worth committing; the raw capture is not.
*/f*.png
*/*.png
*/raw.json
# film mode, added 2026-09-23. One row per animation frame, so a single
# 17k-pixel page is 3.3MB. Regenerable with `ux-crawl <url> --states film`.
*/film.json
# ux-scan output, added 2026-09-26. 100% coverage of every element at every
# 24px, delta-encoded: 708 positions x 25,127 elements on a 17.8k-pixel page
# is 46MB, against a 5.4MB repo. Regenerable with
# `ux-scan <url> --out lenses/<name>`, and reproducible because the capture
# is deterministic at a fixed viewport and step.
*/scan.json
